## Item 1: storytime-bird

File: assets/storytime-bird.ts, new. The bird kind of assets/parts/bird-kind.ts at 0.4 of its size,
copied from assets/messenger-bird.ts. Same body, same options, same size, same clips.

Changes from the source, and nothing else:

- `name`: 'storytime-bird'. `description`: a plain blue songbird, no collar and no tube.
- Slots: `body`, `head`, and `wings` hold one option each, `blue: '#3f6fa8'`; `eyes` holds the
  source `dark: '#2a1a12'`. No presets. The kind requires the four slots, so they stay with one
  option each.
- `colors`: `belly: '#a9c8e8'` (light blue breast) and `flight: '#2f5584'` (the darker shade, on
  the wing tips where the source used its darker wing colour `#a87444`). The feet (`#e88a8a`,
  `#d47878`), the talon colour, and the beak colours `#7a7680` stay as in the source. The eyes are
  unchanged.
- `beakOpen: 18` added: the lower beak turns down about the jaw joint (bird-kind.ts line 445).
- `extra` removed: the leather collar, the brass buckle, the message tube, the rolled letter, and
  the red wax seal are gone. The collar imports are gone with it.
- The cheek paint, the clay surface, the feather bump on the wings, the wing pose, the tail, and
  the six clips stay as in the source.

