## Item 2: look-down cutouts of the pond and the rug

Ordered call, one call:
./forge cutout pond --out out/chibi-sprouts/r1/props-high-xl --ppm 192 --canvas 1024x1024 \
  --views three-quarter --el 35 &&
./forge cutout rug --out out/chibi-sprouts/r1/props-high-xl --ppm 192 --canvas 1024x1024 \
  --views three-quarter --el 35 &&
node scripts/cutout-check.mjs out/chibi-sprouts/r1/props-high-xl

Result: exit 1, both cut off at the bottom edge.

FAIL pond/three-quarter.png  1024x1024 soft 689 edge 567 worstDrop 52% rows 882..1023 cols 282..751
  cut off at the bottom edge (lowest opaque row 1023 of 1024)
FAIL rug/three-quarter.png  1024x1024 soft 851 edge 694 worstDrop 34% rows 916..1023 cols 328..698
  cut off at the bottom edge (lowest opaque row 1023 of 1024)

The water and the rug face did show in both images; the near edge was outside the frame.

Fallback from the order, one call (--ppm 160, folder props-high-xl160): exit 1, both cut off again.

FAIL pond/three-quarter.png  soft 594 edge 480 rows 903..1023  cut off at the bottom edge
FAIL rug/three-quarter.png   soft 721 edge 589 rows 931..1023  cut off at the bottom edge

Cause, measured: a look-down cut sets the ground point on the foot row and the near ground edge
falls below it. The foot row is `canvas height - margin`, and the default margin is 16 px, so 15 px
stay below the ground point. The near edge of a flat prop falls much further. Probe runs:

- /tmp/opencode/probe-m400 (192 px/m, el 35, margin 400): foot row 624; pond rows 498..772, so the
  near edge is 148 px below the ground point; rug rows 532..733, so 109 px below.
- At ppm 160 the same near edge falls 123 px below (118 px for the rug). A lower ppm does not
  remove the cut at the default margin, because the margin does not change with the ppm.

The order cited the lily pad ("as the lily pad"). The lily pad look-down folder is
out/chibi-sprouts/r1/props/high: canvas 1024x1024, elevation 35, footPoint row 874, so a margin of
150 px. A look-down folder stores the foot point in its manifest and the compositor reads it, so
the margin is a framing value of the folder, not a change to the asset or the scale.

Action within the order's fixed values: the rug is cut again at 192 px/m, el 35, canvas 1024x1024,
with `--margin 150` (the lily pad's margin). One call, with the check:

./forge cutout rug --out out/chibi-sprouts/r1/props-high-xl --ppm 192 --canvas 1024x1024 \
  --views three-quarter --el 35 --margin 150 &&
node scripts/cutout-check.mjs out/chibi-sprouts/r1/props-high-xl

Result: exit 0. ok rug/three-quarter.png 1024x1024 soft 1595 edge 1301 worstDrop 39% rows
782..983 cols 328..703; `result ok`. The manifest records footPoint row 874, canvas 1024x1024,
elevation 35, ppm 192. Looked at it once: the red field, the cream border, the medallion, and the
tassels read; the whole rug sits inside the frame.

The pond does not pass at el 35, and the ppm is not the cause. Probe evidence:

- /tmp/opencode/probe-m150 (192 px/m, el 35, margin 150): the pond fits the frame (rows 748..1022)
  but the check fails: `dark halo on 210 of 1118 edge pixels (worst drop 52 %)`.
- The dark edge pixels sit in rows 852..1022, that is, the near rim only. Sample soft pixels hold
  #304513, #3f5a1c, #324715 next to an inner mean of 103..136. These are dark green surface
  colours, not a blend with black, so the cause is the unlit underside of the bank at el 35, not
  the cutout compositing. At el 0 the same asset reported worstDrop 8 %.
- A halo fix needs a change to the pond asset (the bank's underside colour or roughness) or a
  different elevation. The order fixes el 35 and says the pond geometry needs no change.

The pond look-down cutout is therefore not delivered. props-high-xl holds the rug only. The failed
attempts stay as evidence in out/chibi-sprouts/r1/props-high-xl160/ (ppm 160, margin 16) and in
/tmp/opencode/probe-m150 and /tmp/opencode/probe-m400 (scratch).

Tool note for the owner of src/render/page.ts: the cutout fit check tests `minY < 0`, `minX < 0`,
and `maxX > width`, but not `maxY > height`. A look-down cut can lose its near edge without a
"does not fit" message; only cutout-check catches it. This round did not change src/.

## Open question for the orchestrator (blocks the pond cutout)

The pond look-down cutout fails at the ordered settings, and the ordered fallback (ppm 160) does
not fix it. Two decisions belong to the PM:

1. The near rim of the bank is unlit dark green at el 35 (210 of 1118 edge pixels, worst drop
   52 %). Options: (a) a pond asset change (a lighter or rougher bank underside, or a fill light)
   as a new item; (b) a different elevation for the pond look-down only, for example 55, in its
   own folder, which the folder manifest records; (c) accept the halo for this prop and record it.
2. The look-down folder needs `--margin 150` (the lily pad's value), or about 160 px at 192 px/m,
   because the ordered command did not name a margin. The rug is cut at 150. Confirm the value for
   the delivery folder, and confirm that the pond folder uses the same one.

